* TOOL_ACCOUNTS
* The accounts on one screen: every registered account with its kind, whether it is suspended, which gates are on for it and who is signed on in it; and CREATE.ACCOUNT, DELETE.ACCOUNT and
* MODIFY.ACCOUNT (suspend, add or take away a person of a group account) behind a box (S.75, plan .claude/plan-fullscreen-toolkit.md section 5, A3).
* Copyright (c) 2026, SD Core for Linux.  This program is free software; you can redistribute
* it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later.
*
* START-HISTORY:
* 10 Nov 26 Windows port - from Linux (S.75 A3 and its later changes to 9 Nov 26; RELEASE_1.1 221).  OS deviations: the words say Windows users and groups (sdu_ and sdg_); a group
*               account's people are changed by the verb in this elevated session, not through a root helper; X asks no REMOVE.HOME question, because DELETE.ACCOUNT here removes the
*               profile of a Windows user SD made anyway (the keyword is accepted and changes nothing); an OTHER account's directory is a full Windows path; messages 11865 and 14045
*               are 12870 and 15045.
* 25 Oct 26 dm  New.
* 28 Oct 26 dm  S.88 L2: the three boxes are panes of the layout service ($tk_layout): at 140 by 43 exactly the boxes the page has always drawn, in a bigger window the list shows more accounts
*               (twice the share of the box under it, which shows more of what is known about the account under the cursor) and every box is wider.  The resize key makes the layout again,
*               and so does the return from a verb that was given the terminal (the new $tk_open has no panes).
* 1 Nov 26 dm  S.97 stage 2 (group B): the AI line ($tk_aipage), as tool.voc has it: F6 or AI > Ask the AI; refresh is the one action offered to the model (an administrator's
*               page: nothing that changes an account is offered).  An administrator without the AI sees the page as it was.
* 8 Nov 26 dm  S.176: F6 / Shift-F6 are the box keys of every page ($tk_aipage 'ring'): from the list to the AI line and back; AI > Ask the AI is a menu entry of its own.
* 8 Nov 26 dm  S.179: Ctrl-T the theme (View > Theme) and Ctrl-K the keys of the page (Help > Keys), through $tk_std as on every page.
* 9 Nov 26 dm  S.186: View > Mouse and Ctrl-O (the log of the commands run), the same on every page (act:std.mouse, ctrl-o, $tk_std); an account name the page will not put in a command
*              now says which character ($tk_badch).  '/' finds an account by typing ($tk_findrow; the owner: "Letters stay, '/' finds").
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   TOOL.ACCOUNTS      (SDSYS's VOC only; the audience is the administrator, asked of the kernel before anything is read)
*
*   A full-screen page, in the toolkit's frame (140 columns by 43 lines at least).  The top box counts the accounts (users, groups, others), the suspended ones and the sessions signed on.
*   The list is every registered account but SDSYS: its name, its kind, whether it is suspended, the gates that are ON for it (read as TOOL.GATES reads them: the register and the Windows
*   groups, through $tk_gates) and how many sessions are signed on in it.  The box at the foot shows the account under the cursor as !acc_os_info reports it (the Windows user and group, the
*   routes, a group account's members), the gates that are on, and who is signed on in it.  The gate switches themselves are TOOL.GATES's; this page is the account.
*
*   WHAT IT RUNS.  Each through a box that shows the command and what it does, answered Run or Cancel (Cancel is what Enter chooses); the verbs ask for the administrator again and write
*   their own audit lines:
*     S   MODIFY.ACCOUNT name SUSPENDED or UNSUSPENDED    (whichever the account is not; a suspended account is refused at sign-on, by ssh and by the API; nothing changes in Windows)
*     A   MODIFY.ACCOUNT group ADD user                    (a group account only: a Windows user joins its group; a question asks for the user)
*     R   MODIFY.ACCOUNT group DELETE user                 (the same, taking one away)
*     C   CREATE.ACCOUNT GROUP name NO.QUERY, CREATE.ACCOUNT OTHER name path NO.QUERY, and CREATE.ACCOUNT USER name {SSH|API|BOTH|NONE}, for which THE TERMINAL IS GIVEN TO THE VERB, because it
*         asks for the new person's password at a prompt of its own that shows nothing; nothing typed there passes through this page, and you come back to the page when it ends
*     X   DELETE.ACCOUNT name, after the account's name is typed; the terminal is given to the verb for its own question (it has no NO.QUERY and never goes down a pipe)
*   A new account has every gate OFF as the verb makes it; turning one on is TOOL.GATES's.  SDSYS cannot be changed here.
*
*   Keys: Up, Down, PgUp, PgDn, Home, End; S, A, R, C, X as above; F5 reads again; F1 or ? or a click on the [?] explains the page; Ctrl-Q leaves.  A click on a row puts the cursor there.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
program $tool_accounts
$catalog $tool_accounts

$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h
$include err.h
$include sl.h
$include tk.h

   prompt ''

   allow = 'modify.account create.account'                      ;* the commands this page may run through the routines (delete.account and create.account user are run by the verb on the terminal)
   call $tk_open('tool.accounts', 'admin', ctx, err)
   if err # '' then
      display err
      stop
   end
   void kernel(K$AUDIT, 'tool start app=tool.accounts')
   gosub declare.layout

   keys = ''
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f1', 'help', 'help', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'c', 'create', 'create', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 's', 'suspend', 'suspend', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'a', 'add person', 'addperson', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'r', 'take away', 'delperson', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'x', 'delete', 'delete', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, '/', 'find', 'find', '', 1)                  ;* 9 Nov 26 (S.186): '/' finds an account by typing (letters are this page's commands)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f5', 'read', 'refresh', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'ctrl-q', 'quit', 'quit', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'esc', 'menu', 'menu', '', 1)                ;* S.88 U1: Esc opens the menu bar (this page holds nothing of its own that Esc closes first)
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'quit', '&File', '&Quit', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'create', '&Account', '&Create an account', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'suspend', '&Account', '&Suspend or lift', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'addperson', '&Account', '&Add a person to a group account', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'delperson', '&Account', '&Take a person away', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'delete', '&Account', '&Delete the account', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'refresh', '&View', '&Refresh', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'find', '&View', '&Find an account', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'help', '&Help', '&Help on this page', '', '')
   call $tk_std('keys', ctx, keys, '', '')                ;* S.179: Ctrl-T theme, Ctrl-K keys and their View and Help entries, as on every page
   * S.97 stage 2 (group B): the AI line.  The page offers the AI only refresh (an administrator's page: create, delete, suspend and the people are not offered without the
   * owner's word); a proposal is carried out by the page's own key.  This page laid itself out first, so a line that took a row has the panes declared again.
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'refresh', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_aipage('init', ctx, keys, '', '', aout)
   if aout then gosub declare.layout

   ha ='  ' : fmt('Account', '20L') : fmt('Kind', '7L') : fmt('State', '11L') : fmt('Gates that are on', '41L') : fmt('Signed on', '10L') : 'Description'

   an = 0 ; anm = '' ; akind = '' ; asusp = '' ; agates = '' ; asess = '' ; adesc = ''
   nusers = 0 ; ngroups = 0 ; nothers = 0 ; nsusp = 0 ; nsess = 0
   udata = ''
   ci = 1 ; ta = 0
   find.last = ''                                               ;* 9 Nov 26 (S.186): the text '/' asked for last
   gen = 0
   done = 0
   msg = ''

   gosub read.all
   gosub draw.all

   loop
      call $tk_menubar('draw', ctx, keys, 'Accounts', '', '', mr)           ;* the bar first: it writes row 0 whole, and the frame then writes the app name at its right end
      call $tk_frame(ctx, keys, 'Accounts', msg)
      call $sl_curat(0, ctx<TK.C.YSTAT>)
      nm = ''
      screen key returning nm
      mr = ''
      ao = ''
      if nm # '' then call $tk_aipage('key', ctx, keys, 'Accounts', nm, ao)          ;* S.97 stage 2: while the AI line has the focus it takes the keys, before the bar sees them
      if ao<1> = 'replay' then nm = ao<2>                                            ;* an action the AI proposed and the person accepted: this page's own key for it
      if ao<1> # '' then msg = ao<4>
      if nm # '' and ao<1> = '' then call $tk_menubar('key', ctx, keys, 'Accounts', nm, 0, mr)       ;* F10, Alt and a letter, and Esc (nothing of this page's is open): the bar
      if mr<1> # '' then nm = mr<4>
      begin case
         case ao<1> = 'taken'
            if ao<3> then
               gen += 1                                                               ;* the preview, the wait and the answer covered the page: all of it is drawn again
               ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
               gosub draw.all
            end
         case nm = ''
            if status() = ER$EOF then exit
         case nm = 'guardquit'
            exit
         case nm = 'resize'
            call $tk_layout('refresh', ctx, '', lchg)
            gosub get.rects
            gosub keep.in.view
            gen += 1
            ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
            gosub draw.all
         case nm = 'mouse'
            gosub on.mouse
         case 1
            gosub on.key
      end case
      if done then exit
   repeat

   call $tk_close(ctx)
   stop

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- what the machine says

* Every registered account but SDSYS in name order, each with its kind, its suspension, the gates that are on, its description and the sessions signed on in it; the cursor goes back to its account
read.all:
   sel.a = ''
   if an > 0 and ci >= 1 and ci <= an then sel.a = anm<ci>
   names = ''
   openpath @sdsys : @ds : 'accounts' to acc.f then
      select acc.f to 9
      loop
         readnext id from 9 else exit
         if id # 'sdsys' then
            locate id in names<1> by 'AL' setting lp else
               ins id before names<lp>
            end
         end
      repeat
      close acc.f
   end
   call !listu(udata)
   nsess = dcount(udata, @fm)
   an = 0 ; anm = '' ; akind = '' ; asusp = '' ; agates = '' ; asess = '' ; adesc = ''
   nusers = 0 ; ngroups = 0 ; nothers = 0 ; nsusp = 0
   have.reg = 0
   openpath @sdsys : @ds : 'accounts' to acc.f then have.reg = 1
   for i = 1 to dcount(names, @fm)
      call $tk_gates(names<i>, g, ainfo, gerr)
      if gerr = '' then
         an += 1
         anm<an> = names<i>
         akind<an> = ainfo<1>
         asusp<an> = ainfo<2>
         on.list = ''
         for j = 1 to dcount(g, @fm)
            if g<j, 2> = 1 then on.list := (if on.list = '' then '' else ' ') : g<j, 1>
         next j
         agates<an> = on.list
         adesc<an> = ''
         if have.reg then
            read arec from acc.f, names<i> then adesc<an> = arec<ACC$DESCR>
         end
         ns = 0
         for k = 1 to nsess
            if udata<k, 9> = names<i> then ns += 1
         next k
         asess<an> = ns
         begin case
            case ainfo<1> = 'USER'
               nusers += 1
            case ainfo<1> = 'GROUP'
               ngroups += 1
            case 1
               nothers += 1
         end case
         if ainfo<2> = 1 then nsusp += 1
      end
   next i
   if have.reg then close acc.f
   if ci > an then ci = an
   if ci < 1 then ci = 1
   if sel.a # '' then
      for i = 1 to an
         if anm<i> = sel.a then
            ci = i
            exit
         end
      next i
   end
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- drawing

* The layout (S.88 L2).  The three boxes are the panes of the layout service, declared in the sizes of the reference layout (140 by 43, the body 138 by 39): the box at the top stays as
* high as it is, and the rows a bigger window gives are shared by the list (twice) and the box under it (once, which shows more of what is known about the account).  A new $tk_open
* (after the terminal was handed to a verb) has no panes, so the declaration is made again then.
* Out: top (the counts), lst (every account), det (the account under the cursor), each .x .y .w .h; ttw, ltw, dtw (the text width of each box); VA (the account rows on the screen) and
* DR (the rows of the box under the list).
declare.layout:
   ld = ''
   ld<1> = 'counts' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 6 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   ld<2> = 'list' : @vm : 2 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 20 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 2 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   ld<3> = 'detail' : @vm : 3 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 13 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   call $tk_layout('declare', ctx, ld, perr)
   if perr # '' then
      call $tk_close(ctx)
      display perr
      stop
   end
   gosub get.rects
   return

get.rects:
   call $tk_layout('pane', ctx, 'counts', lrc)
   top.x = lrc<1, 1> ; top.y = lrc<1, 2> ; top.w = lrc<1, 3> ; top.h = lrc<1, 4>
   call $tk_layout('pane', ctx, 'list', lrc)
   lst.x = lrc<1, 1> ; lst.y = lrc<1, 2> ; lst.w = lrc<1, 3> ; lst.h = lrc<1, 4>
   call $tk_layout('pane', ctx, 'detail', lrc)
   det.x = lrc<1, 1> ; det.y = lrc<1, 2> ; det.w = lrc<1, 3> ; det.h = lrc<1, 4>
   ttw = top.w - 4
   ltw = lst.w - 4
   dtw = det.w - 4
   VA = lst.h - 3                                               ;* the heading, the account rows and the border: 17 rows of 20
   DR = det.h - 2                                               ;* the rows of the box under the list: 11 of 13
   return

* After a resize the rows scrolled off the top are not more than the accounts listed less the rows that fit
keep.in.view:
   if ta > an - VA then ta = an - VA
   if ta < 0 then ta = 0
   return

draw.all:
   cw2 = ctx<TK.C.W>
   chh = ctx<TK.C.H> - 5
   screen clear at 0,1 size cw2,chh
   screen box at top.x,top.y size top.w,top.h title 'Accounts'
   screen box at lst.x,lst.y size lst.w,lst.h title 'Every account'
   screen box at det.x,det.y size det.w,det.h title 'The account under the cursor'
   gosub draw.top
   gosub redraw
   return

draw.top:
   s = an : ' account' : (if an = 1 then '' else 's') : ': ' : nusers : ' user, ' : ngroups : ' group, ' : nothers : ' other.   Suspended: ' : nsusp : '.   Sessions signed on now: ' : nsess : '.'
   screen text s[1, ttw - 6] at top.x + 2,top.y + 1 attr 'bold' width ttw - 6
   screen text 'SDSYS, the administrator, is not listed and cannot be changed here. The gate switches are TOOL.GATES; a new account has every gate off.' at top.x + 2,top.y + 2 width ttw
   screen text 'C creates an account.  X deletes one (its name is typed first).  S suspends the account under the cursor or lifts the suspension.' at top.x + 2,top.y + 3 width ttw
   screen text 'A adds a person to a group account and R takes one away.  F5 reads again.' at top.x + 2,top.y + 4 width ttw
   call $tk_help('mark', top.x + top.w - 5, top.y + 1, 0, 0)
   return

redraw:
   gosub draw.list
   gosub draw.detail
   return

draw.list:
   screen text ha at lst.x + 2,lst.y + 1 attr 'header' width ltw
   if ci <= ta then ta = ci - 1
   if ci > ta + VA then ta = ci - VA
   if ta < 0 then ta = 0
   for r = 1 to VA
      kk = ta + r
      s = ''
      if kk <= an then
         st.t = (if asusp<kk> = 1 then 'SUSPENDED' else 'active')
         gtxt = agates<kk>
         if gtxt = '' then gtxt = '(none)'
         s = (if asusp<kk> = 1 then '* ' else '  ') : fmt(anm<kk>[1, 19], '20L') : fmt(downcase(akind<kk>), '7L') : fmt(st.t, '11L') : fmt(gtxt[1, 40], '41L') : fmt(asess<kk>, '10L') : adesc<kk>
      end
      rat = 'normal'
      if kk = ci and kk <= an then rat = 'highlight'
      screen text s[1, ltw] at lst.x + 2,lst.y + 1 + r attr rat width ltw
   next r
   return

* The account under the cursor: what !acc_os_info says of it, the gates that are on, and who is signed on in it
draw.detail:
   for r = 1 to DR
      screen text '' at det.x + 2,det.y + r width dtw
   next r
   if an = 0 or ci < 1 or ci > an then
      screen text 'There is no account to show.' at det.x + 2,det.y + 1 width dtw
      return
   end
   nme = anm<ci>
   lines = ''
   openpath @sdsys : @ds : 'accounts' to acc.f then
      read arec from acc.f, nme then
         call !acc_os_info(nme, arec, info, ierr)
         lines<-1> = nme : '   ' : downcase(akind<ci>) : (if asusp<ci> = 1 then '   SUSPENDED' else '   active') : '   path: ' : arec<ACC$PATH>
         if ierr # '' then
            lines<-1> = 'The account facts could not be read.'
         end else
            ln.s = ''
            for k = 1 to dcount(info, @fm)
               ln.s := (if ln.s = '' then '' else '   ') : info<k>
            next k
            call $tk_wrap(ln.s, dtw, pieces)
            lines<-1> = pieces
         end
      end
      close acc.f
   end
   gtxt = agates<ci>
   lines<-1> = 'Gates that are on: ' : (if gtxt = '' then '(none)' else gtxt)
   sn = ''
   for k = 1 to nsess
      if udata<k, 9> = nme then sn := (if sn = '' then '' else ', ') : 'user ' : udata<k, 1> : ' (' : udata<k, 6> : ')'
   next k
   lines<-1> = 'Signed on in it: ' : (if sn = '' then 'nobody' else sn)
   for r = 1 to dcount(lines, @fm)
      if r <= DR then
         lr = lines<r>
         screen text lr[1, dtw] at det.x + 2,det.y + r width dtw
      end
   next r
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- keys and mouse

on.key:
   msg = ''
   if len(nm) = 1 and nm >= 'A' and nm <= 'Z' then nm = downcase(nm)
   begin case
      case nm = 'up'
         if ci > 1 then ci -= 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'down'
         if ci < an then ci += 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = '/'                         ;* S.186: the next account whose name holds the text typed ($tk_findrow)
         call $tk_findrow(anm, ci, find.last, fpos)
         if fpos > 0 then ci = fpos
         if fpos < 0 then msg = sysmsg(15045, find.last)
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'pgup'
         ci -= VA
         if ci < 1 then ci = 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'pgdn'
         ci += VA
         if ci > an then ci = an
         if ci < 1 then ci = 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'home'
         ci = 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'end'
         ci = an
         if ci < 1 then ci = 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'c'
         gosub do.create
      case nm = 's'
         gosub do.suspend
      case nm = 'a'
         sub.word = 'add'
         gosub do.person
      case nm = 'r'
         sub.word = 'delete'
         gosub do.person
      case nm = 'x'
         gosub do.delete
      case nm = 'ctrl-t'                    ;* S.179: the theme, kept for the person - the same on every page ($tk_std)
         call $tk_std('theme', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
         if std.r<1> then gosub draw.all
         msg = std.r<2>
      case nm = 'act:std.mouse'             ;* S.186: View > Mouse, the same on every page ($tk_std)
         call $tk_std('mouse', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
         msg = std.r<2>
      case nm = 'ctrl-o'                    ;* S.186: the log of the commands this page ran (View > Output; $tk_std)
         call $tk_std('output', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
      case nm = 'ctrl-k'                    ;* S.179: the keys of this page, in a box
         call $tk_std('keylist', ctx, keys, 'Accounts', std.r)
      case nm = 'f5'
         gosub read.all
         gosub draw.all
         msg = 'read again'
      case nm = 'f1' or nm = '?'
         call $tk_help('box', 'tool.accounts.page', hm, 0, 0)
         if hm # '' then msg = hm
      case nm = 'f6' or nm = 'shift-f6' or nm = 'act:ai'
         call $tk_aipage('ring', ctx, keys, 1, nm : @fm : 1, ap)            ;* S.176: F6 / Shift-F6 go round the boxes (one here) and the AI line; AI > Ask the AI goes to the line
         msg = ap<2>
      case nm = 'ctrl-q'
         done = 1
   end case
   return

on.mouse:
   screen mouse returning mev else mev = ''
   if mev = '' then return
   mr = ''
   call $tk_menubar('click', ctx, keys, 'Accounts', mev, '', mr)                  ;* a click on the bar on row 0
   if mr<1> # '' then
      nm = mr<4>
      if nm # '' then gosub on.key                          ;* a bar left with nothing chosen has no name: the status message stays
      return
   end
   call $tk_aipage('mouse', ctx, keys, 'Accounts', mev, ap)                         ;* S.97 stage 2: a click on the AI line gives it the focus
   if ap # '' then
      msg = ap
      return
   end
   call $tk_help('hit', mev, top.x + top.w - 5, top.y + 1, hit.m)
   if hit.m then
      call $tk_help('box', 'tool.accounts.page', hm, 0, 0)
      if hm # '' then msg = hm
      return
   end
   if mev<1> = 'press' and mev<2> = 1 then
      mx = mev<3>
      my = mev<4>
      if mx >= lst.x + 2 and mx <= lst.x + lst.w - 3 and my >= lst.y + 2 and my <= lst.y + 1 + VA then
         if ta + my - lst.y - 1 <= an then
            ci = ta + my - lst.y - 1
            gosub redraw
         end
      end
   end
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the commands

* Is word a safe single word for the routines (a-z, 0-9, dot, dash, underscore, 1 to 32 characters)?  plain is 1 or 0
plain.word:
   plain = (word # '' and len(word) <= 32)
   for pi = 1 to len(word)
      if index('abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789.-_', word[pi, 1], 1) = 0 then plain = 0
   next pi
   return

* sent and el are the sentence and its explanation, typed is null or the word to type; the box is shown, the command run when Run was chosen through $tk_run, everything read again and the verb's words shown
confirm.and.run:
   call $tk_confirm(sent, el, typed, res, cmsg)
   if res = 'run' then
      if use.x then
         call $tk_runx(allow, sent, out, stat, err)
      end else
         call $tk_run(allow, sent, out, stat, err)
      end
      gosub read.all
      gosub draw.all
      if err # '' then
         msg = err
      end else
         msg = sent[1, 60] : ' ran (status ' : stat : ')'
         lastl = ''
         for k = 1 to dcount(out, @fm)
            if trim(out<k>) # '' then lastl = trim(out<k>)
         next k
         if lastl # '' then msg = msg : ': ' : lastl
      end
   end else
      msg = cmsg
   end
   return

* The same box, but when Run is chosen the TERMINAL is given to the verb (it asks its own questions, one of them for a password that is not shown), and the page is taken again afterwards
confirm.and.hand.over:
   call $tk_confirm(sent, el, typed, res, cmsg)
   if res # 'run' then
      msg = cmsg
      return
   end
   call $tk_close(ctx)
   execute sent
   crt
   crt sysmsg(12870) :                                         ;* Press Enter to return
   input junk
   if junk = char(1) then null                                 ;* any answer goes back; the answer itself is not used
   call $tk_open('tool.accounts', 'admin', ctx, err)
   if err # '' then
      display err
      done = 1
      return
   end
   call $tk_aipage('again', ctx, keys, '', '', aout)            ;* S.97 stage 2: the new context has no AI line yet; the account may have changed it in the command
   gen += 1
   ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
   gosub declare.layout                                         ;* the new $tk_open has no panes
   gosub read.all
   gosub draw.all
   msg = 'back from ' : sent[1, 40] : ': the list shows what is registered now'
   return

do.suspend:
   if an = 0 or ci < 1 or ci > an then
      msg = 'there is no account'
      return
   end
   word = anm<ci>
   gosub plain.word
   if not(plain) then
      call $tk_badch(word, bad.ch)                   ;* 9 Nov 26 (S.186): say which character
      if bad.ch = '' then bad.ch = 'more than 32 characters'
      msg = 'this account name has ' : bad.ch : ', which this page will not put in a command; use modify.account at the prompt'
      return
   end
   use.x = 0
   typed = ''
   el = ''
   if asusp<ci> = 1 then
      sent = 'modify.account ' : anm<ci> : ' unsuspended'
      el<-1> = 'The suspension of ' : anm<ci> : ' is lifted: the account can be signed on to again, by the console, ssh and the API. Nothing changes in Windows.'
   end else
      sent = 'modify.account ' : anm<ci> : ' suspended'
      el<-1> = anm<ci> : ' is suspended: LOGIN, ssh and the API refuse it from now on. Sessions already signed on in it keep running until they end. Nothing changes in Windows, so lifting it later costs nothing.'
   end
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

* sub.word is add or delete: a Windows user joins or leaves the group of the group account under the cursor
do.person:
   if an = 0 or ci < 1 or ci > an then
      msg = 'there is no account'
      return
   end
   if akind<ci> # 'GROUP' then
      msg = anm<ci> : ' is not a group account: only a group account has people to add or take away'
      return
   end
   word = anm<ci>
   gosub plain.word
   if not(plain) then
      call $tk_badch(word, bad.ch)                   ;* 9 Nov 26 (S.186): say which character
      if bad.ch = '' then bad.ch = 'more than 32 characters'
      msg = 'this account name has ' : bad.ch : ', which this page will not put in a command; use modify.account at the prompt'
      return
   end
   screen ask 'Windows user to ' : (if sub.word = 'add' then 'add to ' else 'take away from ') : anm<ci> : ' (a-z, 0-9, dot, dash and underscore)' width 40 value '' title 'People of a group account' returning pu else return
   word = trim(pu)
   gosub plain.word
   if not(plain) then
      msg = 'a user name has only a-z, 0-9, dot, dash and underscore, up to 32 characters'
      return
   end
   use.x = 0
   typed = ''
   sent = 'modify.account ' : anm<ci> : ' ' : sub.word : ' ' : word
   el = ''
   if sub.word = 'add' then
      el<-1> = word : ' joins the Windows group of ' : anm<ci> : ' and can then enter the account. The group is changed by the verb in this elevated session, as it always does it.'
   end else
      el<-1> = word : ' leaves the Windows group of ' : anm<ci> : ' and can no longer enter the account. Taking access away is always allowed.'
   end
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

* C: the kind, the name, then what that kind needs; a USER account is made with the terminal given to the verb (its password prompt)
do.create:
   * S.88: one form with the four answers in view (it was three questions in a row); a refusal is said under the entries and the form stays
   spec = 'Create an account' : @fm : '&Create' : @fm : ''
   spec<-1> = 'kind' : @vm : 'Kind: user, group, other' : @vm : 10 : @vm : 10
   spec<-1> = 'name' : @vm : 'Name (a-z 0-9 . - _)' : @vm : 34 : @vm : 32
   spec<-1> = 'doors' : @vm : 'Doors: none ssh api both' : @vm : 10 : @vm : 10
   spec<-1> = 'dir' : @vm : 'Directory (other only)' : @vm : 60 : @vm : 200
   fv = 'user' : @fm : '' : @fm : 'none' : @fm : ''
   call $tk_form('open', ctx, spec, fv, fo)
   if fo = 'no' then
      msg = 'the form does not fit this window'
      return
   end
   loop
      call $tk_form('run', ctx, fans, fv, fid)
      if fans # 'ok' then
         call $tk_form('close', ctx, '', '', '')
         return
      end
      kd = downcase(trim(fv<1>))
      word = trim(fv<2>)
      rt = downcase(trim(fv<3>))
      pth = trim(fv<4>)
      fbad = ''
      fid = ''
      begin case
         case kd # 'user' and kd # 'group' and kd # 'other'
            fbad = 'the kind is user, group or other' ; fid = 'kind'
         case 1
            gosub plain.word
            if not(plain) then
               fbad = 'an account name has only a-z, 0-9, dot, dash and underscore, up to 32 characters' ; fid = 'name'
            end else
               locate word in anm<1> setting px else px = 0
               if px > 0 or word = 'sdsys' then
                  fbad = word : ' is already an account' ; fid = 'name'
               end else
                  if kd = 'user' and rt # 'none' and rt # 'ssh' and rt # 'api' and rt # 'both' then
                     fbad = 'the doors are none, ssh, api or both' ; fid = 'doors'
                  end
*                 A full Windows path written with forward slashes, as SD writes its own paths: a drive letter, a colon and '/'.  Not a backslash: $tk_runx refuses one (it
*                 lets no word carry an escape or a quote), so the page asks for the form the command will accept.
                  if kd = 'other' and (not(alpha(pth[1, 1])) or pth[2, 1] # ':' or pth[3, 1] # '/' or index(pth, '\', 1) > 0 or index(pth, ' ', 1) > 0 or len(pth) > 200) then
                     fbad = 'give a full path with forward slashes, such as C:/Data, with no space in it' ; fid = 'dir'
                  end
               end
            end
      end case
      if fbad = '' then exit
      call $tk_form('say', ctx, fbad, fid, '')
   repeat
   call $tk_form('close', ctx, '', '', '')
   nn = word
   use.x = 0
   begin case
      case kd = 'user'
         sent = 'create.account user ' : nn : ' ' : rt
         typed = ''
         el = ''
         el<-1> = 'A Windows user ' : nn : ' (denied the console and Remote Desktop) and the SD account are made, with every gate OFF. The terminal is given to the verb, which asks for the password of the new person (nothing is shown) and for your OK.'
         el<-1> = 'Turning a gate on afterwards is TOOL.GATES. You come back to this page when the verb ends.'
         gosub confirm.and.hand.over
      case kd = 'group'
         sent = 'create.account group ' : nn : ' no.query'
         typed = ''
         el = ''
         el<-1> = 'A group account ' : nn : ' is made: a Windows group (sdg_' : nn : ') for its people and a directory for its files, with no Windows user of its own, so it can have no remote door and no gate that reaches the operating system.'
         el<-1> = 'People are added to it afterwards with A.'
         gosub confirm.and.run
      case 1
         use.x = 1
         sent = 'create.account other ' : nn : ' ' : pth : ' no.query'
         typed = ''
         el = ''
         el<-1> = 'An account ' : nn : ' is made over the directory ' : pth : ', which is not changed. It has no Windows user and no Windows group of its own.'
         gosub confirm.and.run
         use.x = 0
   end case
   return

* X: the account's name is typed, then the terminal is given to DELETE.ACCOUNT for its own question.  No REMOVE.HOME question: on Windows the verb removes the profile of a Windows
* user SD made in any case (the keyword is accepted there and changes nothing).
do.delete:
   if an = 0 or ci < 1 or ci > an then
      msg = 'there is no account'
      return
   end
   word = anm<ci>
   gosub plain.word
   if not(plain) then
      call $tk_badch(word, bad.ch)                   ;* 9 Nov 26 (S.186): say which character
      if bad.ch = '' then bad.ch = 'more than 32 characters'
      msg = 'this account name has ' : bad.ch : ', which this page will not put in a command; use delete.account at the prompt'
      return
   end
   sent = 'delete.account ' : anm<ci>
   typed = anm<ci>
   el = ''
   el<-1> = 'DELETE ' : anm<ci> : ': its directory, its Windows group and its register record are removed' : (if akind<ci> = 'USER' then ', and the Windows user and its profile too when SD made it (one SD did not make is left in place and the verb says so)' else '') : '.'
   el<-1> = 'There is no taking this back. The terminal is given to the verb, which asks once to confirm; then you come back to this page.'
   gosub confirm.and.hand.over
   return

end

